-46b5-ad31-175bf1989bb6)) (rectangle (start 20 209) (end 172 291) (stroke (width 0.2) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid afd5474b-f17a-48ea-adca-ce3b8f66237e)) (text "MOTION: MPU-6050 6-axis IMU on I2C" (at 21.5 212 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) bold) (justify left)) (uuid 3fda273a-ae17-43c9-a031-193404619eba)) (rectangle (start 178 209) (end 330 357) (stroke (width 0.2) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid 72485f30-5c0e-468b-8707-3fcf740812e5)) (text "LIGHT: six WS2812B-Mini pixels (daisy chain), each with 100 nF" (at 179.5 212 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) bold) (justify left)) (uuid 1fb3f538-dfaf-4fc5-91d8-312882ad9258)) (rectangle (start 20 363) (end 172 445) (stroke (width 0.2) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid 7ebc307f-2d7c-429d-8dfa-1a5b155e5a86)) (text "TRIGGER, SOUND, HAPTIC" (at 21.5 366 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) bold) (justify left)) (uuid 1514cc14-4c55-4fce-a857-c97b5483b9a3)) (text "ASTRADAND: hold the trigger, draw a shape in the air, release. The 6-axis IMU is read over I2C at 50 Hz; the ATmega matches the drawn path against six spell templates. Piezo is driven differentially from OC1A/OC1B (D9/D10). LEDs are fed from +4V5 through a high-side switch (Q3, driven by Q4 from D5) and a Schottky (D20), so the pixels draw nothing in sleep so that their 0.7 x VDD data threshold stays below the 3.3 V logic level; the firmware caps the pixel current." (at 20 300 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left)) (uuid 03c21853-69cb-40d1-bb4b-7f0ce076bb06)) (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1"))))